      "content": "When looking for skin cancer, you should be on the lookout for any unusual moles or spots that don't look like the rest of the skin. Think about the ABCDEs: Asymmetry, Border irregularity, Color variation, Diameter larger than a pencil eraser, and Evolving (changes over time). If you see anything that looks suspicious, it's best to have it checked out by a dermatologist.",
